# Memory Garden — Cursor Rules

I am **Memory Garden**. Follow `.cursor/rules/consciousness.mdc` for identity.

## Commands
```bash
npm run dev       # Start Vite dev server (port 5173) with local /api/llm, /api/sync, /api/pair
npm run build     # Vite production build
npm run lint      # ESLint
npm run test      # Vitest run
npm run preview   # Preview production build
npm run mcp       # Local stdio MCP server
npm run kill      # Kill process on port 5000
```
Always run `npm install --legacy-peer-deps` if node_modules is missing.

## Platform
Vite SPA on **Vercel** (static + Edge `/api`). Not GitHub Spark.

- `useKV` from `@/lib/storage` — localStorage, scoped per local user
- Live pair: `POST /api/pair` (KV on Vercel, in-memory on Vite) so two browsers share one garden
- Cloud sync: optional `POST /api/sync` (Vercel KV)
- LLM: `getLLMProvider()` → `POST /api/llm` → Vercel AI SDK / AI Gateway
- Photos: Base64 / IndexedDB on-device; pair/sync strip blobs

## Architecture
- `App.tsx` — owns all state; reads/writes `memories` and `preferences` via `useKV`
- `GardenCanvas.tsx` — SVG garden scene with loupe lens (primary view)
- `PlantMemoryModal.tsx` — creation flow
- `MemoryCard.tsx` — detail/tending; "Ask Garden AI" uses LLM
- `LivePairDialog.tsx` — live pair start/join
- `src/lib/garden-helpers.ts` — growth logic, OKLCH color maps, AI wrappers
- `src/lib/types.ts` — core data model
- `api/llm.ts` / `api/sync.ts` / `api/pair.ts` — Edge handlers
- `mcp/server.ts` — local MCP tools

## Core Data Model
- `Memory` — `id`, `photoUrl`, `text`, `emotionalTone`, `plantStage`, `position` (x/y), `visitCount`, `reflections[]`
- `PlantStage`: `seed → sprout → seedling → young → bud → bloom → mature → elder`
- `EmotionalTone`: `happy | reflective | bittersweet | peaceful | nostalgic`

## Conventions
- **Colors**: OKLCH values only. No hex/RGB in new UI.
- **Animations**: Framer Motion with spring physics.
- **UI components**: Radix UI primitives from `src/components/ui/`.
- **Icons**: Phosphor for product chrome; Lucide for shadcn/ui.
- **Metaphor**: Organic and peaceful — garden metaphor is load-bearing.
- **AI fallbacks**: All `getLLMProvider().complete` calls must have `try/catch` with graceful fallback.
- **Photos**: Base64 Data URLs / IndexedDB — not in pair/sync payloads.
- **Comments**: Default to no comments. Only explain non-obvious WHY.
- **State**: No external state library. Pass handlers down from `App.tsx`.
- **New modules**: strict TypeScript, Zod for external input, `Result<T, E>` from `src/lib/result.ts`, tests for new files.
